// # MCP Subsystem — Anchor for Agents
//
// Logline: Front door for the mcp/ directory. Re-exports the engine facade plus the cli/ command interface, qa, scripts, docs, examples, and audit.
//
// Setup: Pure structural file. The 6 functional subdirs live under engine/ (core, tool, health, federation, state, resource); the engine/ facade re-exports them. The 6 sibling dirs (cli, qa, scripts, docs, examples, audit) provide the OPM tactical-subsystem template surfaces.
//
// Beats:
//   1. engine/ is the only library surface: 6 functional subdirs.
//   2. cli/ is the standalone entry: the mcp binary (stdio server) and mcp-merge (agent-config writer).
//   3. Each engine subdir has its own ANCHOR.oo front door.
//   4. qa/ has 6 self-test probe drivers; scripts/ has build, test, verify, release.
//   5. docs/ has MCP_SETUP.oot, protocol.oot, and client_config.oot; examples/ has 3 sample JSON-RPC requests.
//   6. audit/ has the per-version deep-dive audit history (moved from openOODA/audit/).
//   7. VERSION declares mcp=0.6.0 with ooda compat range and api_surface=7.

import "engine/ANCHOR.oo";
import "cli/ANCHOR.oo";
import "qa/ANCHOR.oo";
import "scripts/ANCHOR.oo";
import "docs/ANCHOR.oo";
import "examples/ANCHOR.oo";
import "audit/ANCHOR.oo";
